<title>USA: Applied Power says outlook 'optimistic'.</title>
<headline>Applied Power says outlook 'optimistic'.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE, Wis. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Applied Power Inc said Wednesday it has an &quot;optimistic outlook&quot; for the rest of fiscal 1997 and into 1998.</p>
<p>Earlier, Applied Power reported earnings for the second quarter ended February 28 of $0.66 a share, up from $0.55 a year ago.</p>
<p>&quot;The earnings per share improvement represents our 13th consecutive quarter of year-over-year EPS growth of 20 percent of better,&quot; Richard Sim, chairman, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sales for the second quarter rose to $157.2 million from $137.1 million.</p>
<p>&quot;We are particularly encouraged by the strengthening trend in orders and sales and we have an optimistic outlook for the rest of 1997 and into 1998,&quot; Sim said in a statement.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
